title: "Quantitative multi-instance extraction from ordinary seeded extractors"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yongxian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3864-3536"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-27
repository-code: "https://github.com/mxym/math"
abstract: "Proves that a strong seeded extractor can produce jointly near-uniform outputs on many coordinates of an arbitrarily correlated block source, given independent seeds and explicit threshold and error conditions. Includes a counterexample to the threshold-free conjecture."
